One Suggestion for Your Folder Structure

Your structure is already strong, but I'd make one improvement.

Instead of:

database/
    models/

I recommend:

modules/

restaurants/
    restaurant.model.ts

orders/
    order.model.ts

menu/
    menu.model.ts

Each module contains its own:

Model
Controller
Service
Routes
Validation
DTO
Constants
Tests

This is a feature-based (domain-driven) structure. It keeps everything related to one business capability together, making the project easier to maintain as it grows.

Development Rules (Do Not Break These)
Never skip validation.
Never access the database directly from controllers.
Keep business logic in services.
Use consistent API response formats.
Handle errors centrally.
Log important actions.
Enforce RBAC before business logic.
Filter all tenant data by restaurantId.
Write clear comments only where they add value.
Complete one module before starting the next.
